  "result": "I added `click.KeyValue`, and it works as specified. The 8 new tests pass, along with the rest of the test suite (1914 passed, 102 skipped).\n\n```python\n@click.option(\"--set\", type=click.KeyValue())\n```\n\n**How it behaves:**\n- `a=b` becomes `(\"a\", \"b\")`.\n- It splits on the first `=` only, so `a=b=c` becomes `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`.\n- An empty value is allowed: `a=` becomes `(\"a\", \"\")`.\n- Input with no `=` (like `ab`) or with an empty key (like `=b`) fails with a usage error: `'ab' is not a valid key=value pair.`\n- If the value is already a 2-item tuple (for example a `default=(\"a\", \"b\")`), it's passed through unchanged.\n- It works with `multiple=True`, so `dict(kv)` gives you a mapping of all the `--set` values.\n- Spaces around the key and value are kept, not trimmed.\n\n**Where the changes are:**\n- `src/click/types.py`: the new `KeyValue` class, placed next to the UUID type.\n- `src/click/__init__.py`: makes it available as `click.KeyValue`.\n- `tests/test_types.py`: tests for valid input, invalid input and `multiple=True`.\n- Docs: an entry in `docs/api.md` and in the built-in types list in `docs/parameter-types.md`.\n- `CHANGES.md`: I started a new \"Version 8.6.0 \u2014 Unreleased\" section, because 8.5.0 is already marked as released. The class docstring also says `versionadded:: 8.6`, so change both if this is going into a different version.\n\nNothing has been committed yet.",
